      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's profoundly disheartening to watch someone try and fail to escape those deep-seated patterns, and that hopelessness is completely understandable. When the tide feels that strong, the idea of fighting it seems futile and draining. Perhaps instead of trying to stop the whole tide, consider finding a way to build a small, personal raft—a small boundary or habit that allows you to float differently, even if the current remains powerful. That tiny act of self-preservation can be a subtle but crucial shift in your narrative.",
      "source": "target",
